    "field": "Snow climatology",
    "problem": "This paper addresses the challenge of establishing cohesive, large-scale trends in Northern Hemisphere snow extremes, which is complicated by the regional nature of most studies, their mixed findings, and the limited availability of station data, particularly for Eurasia and high latitudes.",
    "method": "This paper assesses trends in snow characteristics by reviewing recent studies and performing an original analysis of maximum seasonal snow depth using an area-weighted hemispheric time series created from gridded, standardized station data.",
    "task": "The task is to evaluate trends and extremes in Northern Hemisphere snow characteristics by reviewing recent studies and analyzing observational data for metrics such as snow cover extent, maximum snow depth, and snow water equivalent.",
